WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.675
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:09.408
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:16.691
Unit twenty-eight: Past Simple (irregular verbs). Today you will use common irregular verbs for the past.

4
00:00:16.991 --> 00:00:19.516
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.723
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:25.352
Went.

7
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.199
Went means the past of go.

8
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:30.098
I went to the market.

9
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:32.732
Your turn. Say: Went.

10
00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:36.370
Went.

11
00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:37.932
Saw.

12
00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:40.812
Saw means the past of see.

13
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:42.789
She saw a big bird.

14
00:00:43.383 --> 00:00:45.316
Your turn. Say: Saw.

15
00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.237
Saw.

16
00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:50.706
Ate.

17
00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.368
Ate means the past of eat.

18
00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:55.600
We ate rice for lunch.

19
00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:58.441
Your turn. Say: Ate.

20
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.011
Ate.

21
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:03.496
Had.

22
00:01:04.483 --> 00:01:06.239
Had means the past of have.

23
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:08.269
I had a great weekend.

24
00:01:08.883 --> 00:01:11.478
Your turn. Say: Had.

25
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:15.044
Had.

26
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:16.459
Took.

27
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.171
Took means the past of take.

28
00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:21.051
He took the bus.

29
00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.768
Your turn. Say: Took.

30
00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:27.205
Took.

31
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:28.649
Came.

32
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.301
Came means the past of come.

33
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:33.231
She came home late.

34
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:36.225
Your turn. Say: Came.

35
00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:39.940
Came.

36
00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:41.708
Irregular.

37
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:45.390
Irregular means not following the normal rule.

38
00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:47.635
Go is an irregular verb.

39
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.775
Your turn. Say: Irregular.

40
00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:54.669
Irregular.

41
00:01:55.417 --> 00:01:56.557
Past form.

42
00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.931
Past form means the version of a verb that talks about the past.

43
00:02:01.517 --> 00:02:03.412
Went is the past form of go.

44
00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:06.715
Your turn. Say: Past form.

45
00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.800
Past form.

46
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.297
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.810
Visal, did you say 'I goed to the market' or 'I went to the market'?

48
00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:29.867
I went to the market. Go is an irregular verb. Its past form is went, not goed. Many common verbs are irregular, so we must learn them.

49
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:32.902
Can you give me some other examples?

50
00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:44.969
See becomes saw. Eat becomes ate. Have becomes had. Take becomes took. Come becomes came. There is no rule, so practise the most common ones.

51
00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:47.351
How can we learn them?

52
00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:58.283
Make lists and use them in sentences. I went to the market and saw my friend. We ate rice and had tea. The past form is the same for all subjects.

53
00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:00.887
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:05.236
Grammar focus: Irregular past simple verbs.

55
00:03:05.536 --> 00:03:06.804
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.517 --> 00:03:08.878
I went to the market.

57
00:03:09.783 --> 00:03:11.133
She saw a big bird.

58
00:03:12.017 --> 00:03:13.447
We ate rice for lunch.

59
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:23.206
Irregular verbs have their own past forms: go, went; see, saw; eat, ate; have, had; take, took; come, came. Do not add -ed.

60
00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:27.566
Be careful! Don't say: I goed to the market.

61
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.267
Say: I went to the market.

62
00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:33.683
Go is irregular: went.

63
00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:37.131
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.933 --> 00:03:39.039
Last Weekend.

65
00:03:39.339 --> 00:03:42.372
Last Saturday I went to the market with my mother.

66
00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.912
We saw many fruits and ate some mangoes.

67
00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.830
At home we had tea and took a rest.

68
00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:52.193
My cousin came to visit us in the afternoon.

69
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.652
We learned that many common verbs are irregular.

70
00:03:56.767 --> 00:04:00.652
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:01.517 --> 00:04:03.342
I blank to the park yesterday.

72
00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:06.518
A, goed. B, went. C, go.

73
00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:11.962
The answer is B: went.

74
00:04:13.117 --> 00:04:14.687
She blank a big bird.

75
00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:18.210
A, saw. B, seed. C, sees.

76
00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.697
The answer is A: saw.

77
00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:26.687
They blank rice for lunch.

78
00:04:26.987 --> 00:04:29.979
A, eated. B, eat. C, ate.

79
00:04:33.533 --> 00:04:35.928
The answer is C: ate.

80
00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:38.677
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:38.977 --> 00:04:43.710
A, He taked a bus.. B, He took a bus.. C, He take a bus..

82
00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.998
The answer is B: He took a bus..

83
00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.102
According to the reading, who came in the afternoon?

84
00:04:54.402 --> 00:04:58.427
A, my cousin. B, my mother. C, my friend.

85
00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:04.233
The answer is A: my cousin.

86
00:05:05.433 --> 00:05:08.364
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:09.217 --> 00:05:13.190
Write two sentences about last weekend using irregular past verbs.

88
00:05:21.983 --> 00:05:23.368
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:23.668 --> 00:05:37.758
Last weekend I went to the beach and I saw many boats. We ate fish and had fresh coconut. These sentences use irregular verbs: go became went, see became saw, eat became ate and have became had.

90
00:05:38.058 --> 00:05:39.942
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:45.615
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and irregular past simple verbs.

92
00:05:45.915 --> 00:05:50.460
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

93
00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.703
See you in Unit twenty-nine. Goodbye!

94
00:05:54.003 --> 00:05:56.469
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

